# Build context for services/api/Dockerfile. The context is the workspace root
# because uv.lock lives here; this file is what stops that from meaning
# "upload node_modules and the whole git history to the builder".
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs only four paths, so most entries below are about context
# transfer size and about never letting a secret enter a build layer at all.

# Secrets. Never in an image layer -- Fly reads them from `fly secrets`,
# Vercel from its project settings. See docs/deployment.md.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.github

# The web app deploys to Vercel, not into this image.
node_modules
apps
package.json
package-lock.json

# Host virtualenv: wrong platform, and would shadow the builder's /app/.venv.
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# Nothing the running service reads.
docs
evals
benchmarks
infra
scripts
supabase
*.md
.vscode
.idea
.claude
